--- body ---
## Context

Author decision (Imagine, 2026-11-09, CNRS session on the RDJHSS data
paper release): grow `/submission-event` into the one manuscript
lifecycle skill, with one checklist per stage, and rename it `/paper`
(one syllable, the verb of the dragon, fits every stage including a rejection: the paper is still flying; chosen 2026-11-09 over soar, cran, fledge, clic).
Option A of the design discussion; B (one skill per stage) rejected as
multiplication, C (chapter-only fix) kept as a complement, done in the
CNRS project.

Reference: REALF How-to 44 « Clean up after acceptance / publication »
(`~/CNRS/papiers/actif/REALF 2025 édition/main.pdf`, p. 62) is the
author's own checklist; the skill is derived from the harness
infrastructure, the chapter is its rationale, not its text.

Worked example for the `published` stage: the 2026-11-09 release of the
climate finance corpus data paper (RDJHSS 10, 1–15, DOI
10.52024/fn48qf66). Steps actually needed, none of them in any skill:
dated release subfolder with the publisher PDF and the publication mail;
move `papiers/sent/` → `papiers/published/`; swap the hosted preprint
for the publisher's PDF under the same filename when the license allows;
check the publisher's HTML metadata against the PDF (the landing page
dropped "Multi-Source" from the title); Zotero indexing of supporting
material and informing co-authors as author-only items to ask about.
Memory: `~/.claude/projects/-home-haduong-CNRS/memory/reference-realf-howto-44-release-checklist.md`.

## Design

- `skills/paper/SKILL.md` is a short router: argument `<paper> <event>`,
  the register question first (homepage = works, roadmap = work in
  progress, never both automatically), then load
  `references/<event>.md`. Lifecycle starts at submission; venue choice
  stays with `/choose-venue` and `/conference-submission-prep`.
- `references/` holds one checklist per event: `submitted`,
  `decision-received`, `resubmitted`, `accepted`, `published`. Each
  checklist states: register(s) touched; provenance step (find the
  authentic artifact at its source, hash it; the July 2026 feedback
  memory on reconstructed artifacts); the filesystem steps per the CNRS
  filing convention (dated release subfolders, sent → published);
  outward gates named explicitly with who clicks (`make sync`, HAL
  SWORD via `/update-publist`); delegates (`/ingest-decision-letter`
  for decisions, `/update-publist` for page and HAL); author-only items
  listed so they are asked, not dropped.
- Rename everywhere the name is referenced (`skills-catalog.md`,
  `rules/README.md` line 125, projections, tests). Keep the old name as
  nothing: no alias, the catalog is the lookup.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] An AGENTS.md in ~/CNRS/papiers/ holds what is local (conventions, places, preferences), the skill reads it and holds only the stages, routing and gates. Moves the filing convention out of the memory file `project-cnrs-filing-convention.md` into the directory.
- [ ] `skills/paper/SKILL.md` exists, `skills/submission-event/` is gone, catalog and rules/README updated, hygiene tests pass
- [ ] Five stage checklists in `skills/paper/references/`, each with the sections above
- [ ] The `published` checklist reproduces the 2026-11-09 steps and would have left nothing for the agent to discover
- [ ] `/paper <paper> published` dry run on the data paper lands on "nothing to do except HAL" (positive control)
- [ ] `make check` passes

